219 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 189 0 R
/E (  A low-cost backup release for acoustic receivers on a lake bottom. It sleeps for months, wakes on a set date, listens for one coded tone, and when it hears the tone it powers a hold magnet that lets go of a marker float. The float carries a haul rope to the surface and someone in a boat hauls the receiver up.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
220 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 189 0 R
/E (This guide walks through building one, testing it on a bench, and getting it ready to deploy. It was written by an FLL team \(Coding Curators\) and is a work in progress. Steps we have not tested yet are marked UNTESTED or TBD so you know what to check yourself.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
